    "focal_turn_index": 2,
    "prior_context": {
      "alternative_citation_allowed": true,
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 1 USER]\ne001\tI run product for a nine-person software company.\ne002\tOne of our oldest customers, Northline, wants a reporting workspace that is quite different from what we planned this quarter.\ne003\tThey are not threatening to leave, but their operations lead keeps saying it would make the product usable across the rest of their team.\ne004\tMeanwhile we have reliability work we have postponed twice, and we told smaller customers that the next release would simplify the core workflow.\ne005\tI keep moving between “this is how good products learn” and “we are letting the loudest customer set the roadmap.”\n[Turn 1 ASSISTANT]\ne006\tThe immediate distinction is whether Northline is revealing a broader need or buying influence over a small team.\ne007\tI would not decide from the size of the account alone.\ne008\tAsk what exact job the workspace enables, what they do today, and which parts could serve other customers.\ne009\tIn parallel, make the reliability and roadmap cost visible.\ne010\tIf the request consumes the same people who own those commitments, “we can probably fit it in” is already a choice to delay them.",
